  "interpretation": [
    "The actual job handle was observed only after successful AssignProcessToJobObject. The observer forwarded the original call unchanged.",
    "A controlled native shell was a member of that job in both command/exec and actual codex exec tool paths, on the pinned CLI and current Windows host.",
    "Forced parent execution timeouts also stopped the observed child; the same retained process handle and native creation time were used for verification.",
    "In two serial no-op/write pairs, the 8388608-byte file payload added exactly 8388608 observed write-transfer bytes above the six-byte control marker.",
    "QueryInformationJobObject class 8 includes previously associated processes; the controlled Python writer had already exited before the after-write observation.",
    "The observations support development of a polled cumulative write-I/O budget; they do not establish a hard filesystem or allocated-space quota."
  ],
